#X text 261 93 We now check [lop~] \, [lop2~] (1-pole filters) plus [hip~] \, [hip2~] and [lop3~] (1-Pole and 1-Zero filters). All of them fit into a biquad system (which is a 2-Pole and 2-Zero filter)., f 82;
#X text 261 143 Hence \, we can calculate coefficients and use [biplot] to plot the filter response. Open [pd filters] and compare the examples inside to the one here with [biquad~]. When you set the frequency slider of one of the filters \, like [lop2~] \, [biquad~] will correspond to it and you can see the response below., f 82;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 6 0 0 0;
#X connect 7 0 2 0;
#X connect 7 0 6 0;
